OL,3,AHuawei found guilty of stealing trade  
OL,4,Asecrets but acquitted of racketeering  
OL,6,FHuawei has been found guilty of        
OL,7,Fconspiracy to steal trade secrets and  
OL,8,Fbank fraud, but not guilty of the more 
OL,9,Fserious overarching racketeering charge
OL,10,Fin a landmark case in the US.          
OL,12,FIn a two-month trial, prosecutors      
OL,13,Faccused the Chinese technology and     
OL,14,Ftelecommunications giant of lying,     
OL,15,Fcheating and stealing to gain any      
OL,16,Fcompetitive advantage.                 
OL,18,FHuawei's defence team argued that      
OL,19,Fprosecutors had decided Huawei was a   
OL,20,Fcriminal organisation and built its    
OL,21,Fcase from there, but the firm's success
OL,22,Fwas due to its own innovation.         
